      en: "The Hierophant sits between two pillars in a temple, two students listening before him. His hand is raised in blessing, and his knowledge is inherited — passed from generation to generation, tested, durable. He isn't interested in originality at any cost. He's interested in what actually works. Before him lie two crossed keys — to outer knowledge, and to inner knowledge, to what is learned and to what is awakened.\n\nWhen this card appears, it can speak of mentorship, formal education, faith, or a community offering you belonging. Maybe it's time to find a guide, a teacher, or a system you don't have to build from scratch. Not every path is walked alone. Some are easier walked in line behind someone who's already made the journey.\n\nThe Hierophant's shadow is blindly following rules even when they no longer serve — tradition for tradition's own sake, not because it still makes sense. This card's real wisdom isn't in submission; it's in recognizing which knowledge from the past is worth carrying forward, and which it's time to set down.\n\nIn relationships, the Hierophant can signal a formal commitment — a marriage, a vow, public recognition of a bond, or simply a relationship built on shared values. At work, it speaks of structured learning, a certification, a mentor who can save you years of wandering alone. Don't be ashamed to ask for help from someone who's already walked the path. That isn't weakness. It's wisdom.",
